---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Picture from '../components/Picture.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import { path } from '../data/site';
---
<Layout title="Pardus for business" description="Considered travel coordination for executives and teams, with flights, stays and schedules brought together around business needs.">
  <section class="feature-intro"><div class="feature-intro-content"><p class="eyebrow">Pardus for business</p><h1>Time matters.<br />Travel <em>well.</em></h1><p>Travel coordination for the people moving your business forward. Considered around the agenda, with attention to the person behind it.</p></div><Picture name="corporate" alt="A refined aircraft cabin with comfortable seating" eager /></section>
  <section class="destination-essay section-wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">A considered business journey</p><h2 data-reveal>More focus.<br />Fewer moving <em>parts.</em></h2></div><div class="essay-copy"><p data-reveal>Work travel is different. Arrival times, meeting locations and changing priorities all matter. Pardus helps bring flights, accommodation and ground arrangements into a practical itinerary.</p><p data-reveal>Begin with your schedule, traveller preferences and company requirements. Service arrangements, availability and any ongoing support are agreed for your organisation before travel is confirmed.</p><a class="text-button" href={`${path('journey.html')}?style=Corporate%20travel`} data-reveal>Prepare a corporate travel brief <Arrow /></a></div></section>
  <section class="detail-highlights section-wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Built around your business</p><h2 data-reveal>From the first meeting<br />to the journey <em>home.</em></h2><ol class="process-list"><li data-reveal><span>01</span><div><h3>Executive travel</h3><p>Flights, well-placed accommodation and ground connections shaped around the purpose of the visit.</p></div></li><li data-reveal><span>02</span><div><h3>Teams & groups</h3><p>Coordinate traveller preferences and shared schedules for meetings, events and business journeys.</p></div></li><li data-reveal><span>03</span><div><h3>Clear arrangements</h3><p>Discuss budgets, approval processes and itinerary needs at the beginning, so expectations are agreed.</p></div></li></ol></section>
  <section class="corporate-frame section-wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">A working frame</p><h2>Built around<br /><em>the agenda.</em></h2><p>Start with the non-negotiables, then bring comfort and preference into the space that remains.</p></div><dl><div><dt>01 / Schedule</dt><dd>Meeting locations, arrival windows and fixed commitments establish the route.</dd></div><div><dt>02 / Traveller</dt><dd>Cabin, stay, transfer and communication preferences are captured once and considered together.</dd></div><div><dt>03 / Approval</dt><dd>Budget responsibility, approvers and any company requirements are clarified before confirmation.</dd></div><div><dt>04 / Support</dt><dd>The agreed contact route, change process and service boundaries are documented for each arrangement.</dd></div></dl></section>
</Layout>
